TELOMERE-CCC2-1:{"chunk":"c11","format":"ccc2-wire/1","records":[{"buys":"the arithmetic lives in the deformation/weights -- exactly D4's conclusion, now with the obstruction explained; the D4<->D6 loop is closed","checksum":"82eb81f0ebba4de3f9dfb91c36d18b130caa8d0b549e9b099561bf3335c045c4","id":"B1","limits":"exact constructions only; numerics = hygiene. A conceptual identification (D2 numerics cover it), not a new theorem","type":"B","x":"face-weights as differentiated residues (14c)","y":"Figueiredo's *deformations* (D6) as the mechanism"},{"buys":"the borrowed machine runs on fuel one convolution (Lam=mu*log) from your weights -- a genuine connection, neither fully yours nor fully borrowed","checksum":"8731adfa8493417d7a064e74858cc984bfb0d4081bece217c3ffce1f41889bc8","id":"B2","limits":"the machine (D_log, even/odd blocks, variational principle) is borrowed from CCM; the eigenvalue<->zero identification is numerical, not derived","type":"B","x":"CCM's Lam input (von Mangoldt, on prime powers)","y":"the face-sum's native mu weights (on squarefree subsets)"},{"checksum":"5c10295b2d20ac6ca9ef80118dc14d501daa70e67a960b4845260462906f6948","id":"C1","kind":"claim","label":"Simplicial sieve Delta_z (faces = squarefree products, face-sum Moebius/inclusion-exclusion): NO prior art found","note":"Prior-art search 2026-09-30 (web). The one 'geometric view of the sieve' in the literature (Iosif, arXiv:1112.5796) is about focal lines in integer division -- unrelated. The classical Moebius-of-a-poset/order-complex connection (Rota) is about chains, not the full simplex on primes with face weights. The framing appears new; the underlying inclusion-exclusion is classical (acknowledged throughout). Re-search before any public claim; novelty language in PAPER_OUTLINE.md must respect these boundaries.","status":"conjectural","type":"C"},{"checksum":"1374e57531fdd3eb9187b216bb6c90e53ba4f15c13e6d8caf97a14cd00cc2994","id":"C2","kind":"claim","label":"Weighted infinite simplex, PNT as 'total weight 1' (w(S)=(-1)^{|S|+1}log(prod S)/prod S, sum_{prod S<=X} w(S)->1): NO prior art found","note":"Prior-art search 2026-09-30 (web). Appears new as a statement; it reframes PNT, does not reprove it. Re-search before any public claim.","status":"conjectural","type":"C"},{"checksum":"84c245d4e1f766b73594486dda806cfa53b0e785ac3df1bde9064511fcd73306","id":"C3","kind":"claim","label":"Deforming the sieve's marking rule R_p, proving the deformed survivors ARE the twin lowers, and deriving 2C_2 as the renormalized total weight of the deformed sieve: NOT found in the literature","note":"The constant and its standard local-density derivation are classical (Hardy-Littlewood 1923); related heuristic sieves exist (e.g. arXiv:2507.03107 f(t;z) analysis). The specific move -- the generative deformation -- appears new; the constant is classical. Re-search before any public claim.","status":"conjectural","type":"C"},{"checksum":"2ca8cdffab40378e9257fe14bc37084195ba8d06a91f8de7cedae759bbe86e74","id":"C4","kind":"claim","label":"Fermionic Fock space over primes: INDEPENDENT PRIOR ART EXISTS","note":"goldenphysicsproject (GitHub, contemporary 2026) independently identifies 'squarefree prime subsets as the natural basis of the finite fermionic prime Fock space' and formalizes CAR structure on prime generators in Lean. Priority is genuinely unclear (both contemporary, theirs is a repo not a publication). The identification (faces = Fock basis, mu = fermion parity) is NOT unique to this work and must be credited as independently known. Our distinct contribution is the spectral program: interacting Hamiltonians with arithmetic weights + GUE/Poisson probes (13d/13e) -- no prior art found for that direction.","status":"computationally_verified","type":"C"},{"checksum":"dca40c1d57af263e55e2c7f7941c5bfd74893dd2c7073fdbfb424b04d1811fc4","conventions":["x=10^6; three panels per tuple; NON-ADMISSIBLE {0,2,4} control","code: ktuple_deformation.py; results: ktuple_results.json"],"generates":[{"prescription":"at z=sqrt(x+maxH) compare the deformed survivors against independently enumerated constellation lowers -- exact set match","stage":"survivors (a)"},{"prescription":"compare the finite-z density S(x,30)/x against delta_H(30)=prod(1-nu_p/p)","stage":"density (b)"},{"prescription":"compare the renormalized weight S_H(z) against the reference singular series S(H)","stage":"renormalization (c)"}],"honest_boundary":"(a) at z>=sqrt(x) is essentially definitional (simultaneous Eratosthenes) -- its value is confirming clean generalization plus the non-admissible death, which was the genuinely falsifiable prediction; (b) is classical sieve theory through the deformation lens (confirmatory, not new); (c) reproduces known constants (retrodictive). No new mathematics produced (expected -- it was built to reproduce classical structure). The predictive program's next step is novel deformations (p-dependent R_p), not yet run.","honest_label":"computationally_verified","id":"D1","rule":"for each constellation H, deform R_p to H's forbidden residues; mark n when (n+h) is a PROPER multiple of p<=z (simultaneous Eratosthenes on k linear forms)","subtitle":"k-tuple deformation sweep -- is the deformation a general generative machine or a twin fluke? (PREDICTIVE TEST)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"panel (a): survivors at z=sqrt(x+maxH) vs independently enumerated constellation lowers","expected":"EXACT MATCH on all 9 tuples: twins 8169=8169, sexy 16386, triplets 1393/1444, quad 166, quint 34, sext 5=5 -- zero unsound, zero incomplete"},{"check":"panel (b): finite-z density ratios S(x,30)/x vs delta_H(30)","expected":"0.998-1.015 across all tuples (worst = sext, fewest samples)"},{"check":"panel (c): S_H(1000) vs reference S(H)","expected":"matches ~0.2%: twins/cousins->2C_2, sexy->4C_2 (nu_3=1, factor 2 -- correctly distinguished!), triplets->2.8583, quad->4.1514, quint->10.133, sext->17.301"},{"check":"non-admissible {0,2,4} control","expected":"deformation DIES as predicted -- exactly ONE survivor, n=3 i.e. (3,5,7), the unique prime triple of that form; S_H(z)=0 for z>=3 (nu_3=3 kills the product); the admissibility obstruction emerges from the machine, uninserted"}]},{"checksum":"bb81141b5f7a0778d7f86d5d4bc1bdba7293807598c57d6c0ce62fe1d4e06dbf","generates":[{"prescription":"compute |w({2})| = (log 2)/2 and test membership in {0,1}","stage":"check residues"},{"prescription":"signs are fine (residue alternation); magnitudes impossible -- conclude no ordinary positive geometry","stage":"conclude"}],"honest_boundary":"Explains D4's 'no positive region found' by theorem, not luck. Does NOT forbid deformed homes -- the obstruction is about ordinary positive geometry; 14c constructs the refined home. Recompute via |w({2})|=(log 2)/2 vs {0,1}.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D2","rule":"AHBL canonical forms have logarithmic poles with residues +-1 (0-dim strata: +-1 or 0); |w({2})| = (log 2)/2 = 0.3466 not in {0,1}","subtitle":"14a OBSTRUCTION: no ordinary positive geometry can host the face-weights w(S)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"|w({2})|","expected":"0.3466, not in {0,1}"}]},{"checksum":"cbcab9f3ca545d33fb10c2ad7ac1c818e7b2124ba60983e83438ab09b0eda08b","generates":[{"prescription":"expand the product over subsets of primes <= z","stage":"subset expansion"},{"prescription":"differentiate at u=1 via calculus -- two proofs in DERIVATIONS.md","stage":"differentiate"}],"honest_boundary":"Identity only -- computes the 2^{pi(z)} subset sum in O(pi(z)); says nothing by itself about a geometric home for the weights. Recompute via the product derivative or the subset expansion.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D3","rule":"d/du[prod_{p<=z}(1-p^{-u})]_{u=1} = sum_S w(S) = delta(z)*sum_{p<=z}(log p)/(p-1), with w(S)=(-1)^{|S|+1} log(prod S)/(prod S)","subtitle":"14b IDENTITY: the face-weight sum as a product derivative","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"numeric, z<=29","expected":"verified to 10 digits"},{"check":"asymptotic","expected":"-> e^{-gamma} (0.5333 at z=1e5)"}]},{"checksum":"8cf682804722839899ea5b6ebf6b4005eabc1b175cf1fa06d92d99dd33c14e5f","generates":[{"prescription":"take E_z as the direct sum of line bundles L_p with equivariant Chern roots -u log p (real coefficients, legitimate)","stage":"build bundle"},{"prescription":"form ch(lambda_{-1}(E_z)) = prod(1-p^{-u}) and take the u-derivative at u=1 -- the face-weights emerge as differentiated residues","stage":"differentiate"},{"prescription":"read the geometry: only the primes are input; combinatorics, signs, log-magnitudes computed","stage":"read the geometry"}],"honest_boundary":"Exact constructions; numerics = hygiene. This closes the D4<->D6 loop: the arithmetic lives in the deformation/weights, exactly D4's conclusion, now with the obstruction (14a) explained. It is Figueiredo's *deformations* (D6) as the mechanism -- a conceptual identification (D2 numerics cover it), not a new theorem.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D4","rule":"E_z = (+)L_p with equivariant Chern roots -u*log p; ch(lambda_{-1}(E_z)) = prod(1-p^{-u}); face-weights = u-derivative at u=1 = differentiated residues; positive region = simplex Delta^{m-1} with stringy deformation carrying prime-log exponents","subtitle":"14c REFINED HOME: face-weights as differentiated residues","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"construction","expected":"exact; numerics = hygiene"}]},{"checksum":"d3d9449ac71bcc2da724c1017b86aec05ce8e2668b43f5de70aba75e773331fe","conventions":["use an exact integer cutoff: lam=sqrt(13) float rounding excluded k=13; now 9 prime powers at x=13","restrict to the EVEN subspace (dim N+1): the full matrix at small N shows multiple tiny eigenvalues -- NOT a bug (the known-good connes-cvs CvS implementation shows identical structure at N=8); the even block has the single tiny eigenvalue, the odd block's smallest is 581x larger -- the ground state is naturally even, as the paper assumes","primes ONLY enter via the prime sum (D12 audit boundary); all else is zero-independent analysis"],"generates":[{"prescription":"build M per paper Sec.4 in ccm/ccm_reimpl.py","stage":"assemble"},{"prescription":"restrict to the even block; take the single tiny eigenvalue eps_N by inverse iteration","stage":"isolate ground state"},{"prescription":"normalize delta_N(xi)=1 and read the zeros of xihat(z) from the even-block ground state -- NO zero input anywhere in the pipeline","stage":"extract zeros"}],"honest_boundary":"The machine (D_log, even/odd blocks, variational principle) is BORROWED from CCM; the eigenvalue<->zero identification is numerical, not derived. Higher zeros (4+) require larger N (spurious roots at N=10); systematic N-convergence confirmed. The mechanism is fragile -- see G2. Node 11 stays OPEN as the operator hunt; 11f is the live candidate with an explicit face-sum dictionary entry (Lam=mu*log).","honest_label":"computationally_verified","id":"D5","rule":"M = W_{0,2} - W_R - W_p assembled exactly as paper Sec.4 (arXiv:2511.22755): W_{0,2} verbatim eq.(4.2) [rank 2, verified]; W_R diagonal via master formula (weinfty), validated against direct quadrature to 2e-16; W_R off-diagonal (J(m)-J(n))/(pi(n-m)); prime sum verbatim eq.(bomp) over k=p^r<=lam^2 with von Mangoldt weights","subtitle":"11f: CCM independent reimplementation D_log^{(lam,N)} -- built ONLY from prime Euler products","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"c=13,N=10,dps=60 even block","expected":"single tiny eigenvalue eps_N=2.83e-26 (residual 1.4e-47); odd-block smallest 581x larger (1.64e-23)"},{"check":"zeros, c=13,N=10,dps=60","expected":"zero 1 err 7.1e-15, zero 2 err 2.7e-12, zero 3 err 4.9e-10"},{"check":"c=13,N=20,dps=100","expected":"eps_N=1.57e-39; zeros 1-5 err <4e-11 (zero 1 exact to float64); zeros 6-8 err <1e-6"},{"check":"c=13,N=40,dps=120","expected":"eps_even=9.46e-54; even/odd separation 3744x; zeros 1-5 err <1e-10, 6-10 err <2e-6"},{"check":"N=120 (ccm_largeN.py, 24 min)","expected":"eps_even=3.48e-59, eps_odd=3.06e-55, separation 8771x (monotone 581x->3744x->8771x); zeros 1-5 err <1e-10, zeros 6-10 err <2e-6 -- paper scale matched"}]},{"checksum":"b52e913ed62ba22e46e003238883e70172b4984d51572c0c456fe87d8a311c9a","generates":[{"prescription":"convolve the face-sum's native mu weights (on squarefree subsets) with log to obtain von Mangoldt Lam (on prime powers)","stage":"convolve"}],"honest_boundary":"CCM's fuel is exactly one convolution away from the face-sum's native weights -- the bridge is neither fully yours nor fully borrowed, a genuine connection: the borrowed machine runs on fuel one convolution from your weights. Does not make the machine yours.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D6","rule":"Lam = mu * log (Dirichlet convolution); Lam(n) = -sum_{d|n} mu(d) log d","subtitle":"11f conceptual bridge: CCM's fuel is one convolution from the face-sum's weights","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"numeric, n<5000","expected":"agreement to 3.6e-15"}]},{"checksum":"6f5fba27e5c6c67acf522f167e4c97d1492b532690e64e97ad351d10fb5ce960","id":"G1","result":"A: eps_N=-0.17 (not positive), first root 2.79 (err 11.3). B: eps_N=-0.087, root 5.78 (err 8.4). C: eps_N=0.0175 (not tiny), root 1.16 (err 13.0)","title":"11f CONTROLS: zeros AND positivity both require the precise prime arithmetic","transfer":"the forward-direction test is passed (primes in, spectrum out); this kills the zero-fitting concern on the perturbation direction -- THE question the D12 audit posed (prime-derived Weil-form eigenvectors = principled vs zero-fitted)","tried":"controls at c=13,N=20 (ccm/ccm_controls.py): A (W_p=0), B (shuffled Lam), C (shuffled log p positions)","type":"G","verdict":"the machinery does not produce zeros on its own"},{"checksum":"a88fe72ff471d37c59966c710d5db2e35945d58e7d97497c3b158e58519f0284","id":"G2","result":"multiplicative noise on Lam: 1e-6 -> root err 2.1; 1e-4 -> err 9.2; 1e-2 -> err 11.5 (eps goes negative). Drop p=2 or p=3: destroyed (err ~10.7). Drop p=5: SURVIVES (root 14.063, err 0.07)","title":"11f FAILURE MODES: the mechanism is fragile, not robust","transfer":"the small primes carry the weight (explicit-formula hierarchy); the tiny eigenvalue is a delicate exact-identity cancellation, not a stable gap. Honest scope: a true 'RH false' mapping needs an actual counterexample; what we show is the operator is an exact-arithmetic reporter, not a robust statistical effect","tried":"multiplicative noise on Lam; dropping small primes (ccm/ccm_failure_modes.py)","type":"G","verdict":"fragile exact arithmetic -- not a robust statistical effect"},{"checksum":"c1945427e721c269109540c2462ca6d9661dd980011e4934483d2733bbc82bb2","from":"D2","id":"L1","rel":"supports","to":"V2","type":"L"},{"checksum":"ee82667cd7ec126b9ef5e2dfbdca70ccd5f6b64769b1c648872df75bd3eb116e","from":"D6","id":"L2","rel":"supports","to":"B2","type":"L"},{"checksum":"f1da65af6d8027b7a60476553042d7deb6ec66976790359022daf8bde2a4a7e5","from":"G1","id":"L3","rel":"supports","to":"V3","type":"L"},{"checksum":"0ddacadbe59c211f208f8e0fce04c68b118c591135864238cd347a410cb38b3c","from":"G2","id":"L4","rel":"bounds","to":"V3","type":"L"},{"checksum":"87ef44a3d8208e2aa5dcc07143da02898d47ad912d55c66fee9e5b8af3ed95e4","from":"D5","id":"L5","rel":"supports","to":"V3","type":"L"},{"checksum":"1367e500aa6f0d4fc3084d141034804fd9e171373315440247eb0d04be5dcdcd","consequence":"the deformation is CONFIRMED as a general generative machine, not a twin fluke -- it passed its falsifiable test (the non-admissible {0,2,4} death, which emerged from the machine uninserted). Closed as a confirmation sweep. The predictive program's next step is novel deformations (p-dependent R_p), not yet run. It produced no new mathematics (expected -- it was built to reproduce classical structure).","id":"V1","status":"computationally_verified","subject":"D6-generalization sweep","type":"V"},{"checksum":"b6a18434b4cca3107d4c23dd07ae96d95618ff10181842ecc37d2dc9f56312fb","consequence":"bare complex trivial + weights carry the arithmetic + ordinary positive region impossible (by theorem, 14a) + deformed home constructed (14c). D4's 'no positive region found' is explained, not just recorded.","id":"V2","status":"exact","subject":"Node 14 CLOSED -- D4 fully closed","type":"V"},{"checksum":"5d8dc70bab9eb46017d667536aefc264106466d5d26908b6d88cafd398ee347f","consequence":"the bridge plank EXISTS: primes -> (Weil form) -> zeta zeros, with no zero-fitting in the pipeline. First zeta zero recovered from prime Euler products alone to machine precision. 11f is the live candidate with an explicit face-sum dictionary entry (Lam=mu*log). Node 11 stays OPEN as the operator hunt. Fragility bounds the claim (G2).","id":"V3","status":"computationally_verified","subject":"11f D2 PILOT COMPLETE -- FIRST ZERO RECOVERED from prime Euler products alone","type":"V"}],"registry":{"B1":"B","B2":"B","C1":"C","C2":"C","C3":"C","C4":"C","D1":"D","D2":"D","D3":"D","D4":"D","D5":"D","D6":"D","G1":"G","G2":"G","L1":"L","L2":"L","L3":"L","L4":"L","L5":"L","V1":"V","V2":"V","V3":"V"},"wire_checksum":"044066e25d3487844ef1f2d831538db9ac8c1c0550e4710a0565d12bdb26141f"}:TELOMERE-CCC2-1